// Hand-authored Pine v5 fixture — user-defined function with typed args.
// Pine v5 optionally allows type annotations on function parameters
// as syntactic hints — Phase 1 openbb-pine's grammar treats function
// parameters as untyped tokens (the migration shim keeps the source
// v5-compatible; grammar-level typed-arg support is deferred). This
// fixture therefore uses UNTYPED parameters, which is the more common
// form in real v5 community scripts anyway (per the wild-corpus scan).
// The v5→v6 diff is study() → indicator(); the function definition is
// unchanged.
//
// Per PRD §2.1: hand-authored, not copied from TradingView.
//
// Covers: study() → indicator(), user-defined function with two args,
// custom function calling ta.sma, plot().
//@version=5
study("Custom Function Two Args", overlay=true)
length = input.int(14, minval=1)
weighted(src, len) =>
    basis = ta.sma(src, len)
    basis + src / 2
smoothed = weighted(close, length)
plot(smoothed, title="w", color=color.red)
